{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Of beaten work shall the menorah be made.</b> That he should not make it of rings, nor make its branches and its lamps limb by limb and afterward attach them, in the manner of goldsmiths who are called שולד\"יר בְּלַעַ\"ז, but all of it comes from a single block, and he beats with a hammer and cuts with a craftsman's tool and separates the branches this way and that." "<b>Of beaten work.</b> Its Targum is נְגִיד — a term of drawing, for one draws the limbs from the stock this way and that by beating with the hammer, and מִקְשָׁה means a hammer-blow — בטדי\"ץ בְּלַעַ\"ז, as in ״דָּא לְדָא נָקְשָׁן״ (Daniel 5)." "<b>Shall the menorah be made.</b> By itself — because Moses found it difficult, the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: Cast the ingot into the fire and it is made by itself; therefore it is not written תַּעֲשֶׂה (Tanchuma)." "<b>Its base.</b> That is the leg below, made in the shape of a box, and three legs extend from it downward." "<b>And a branch.</b> Its central branch, which rises from the middle of the base, stands erect upward, and upon it is the central lamp, made in the shape of a basin, to pour the oil into it and to set the wick." "<b>Its goblets.</b> They are like cups made of glass, long and narrow, and they are called מדיר\"נש בְּלַעַז — but these are made of gold, protruding and emerging from every branch, every branch, in the number that Scripture gives for them, and they served only for ornament." "<b>Its knobs.</b> They were like apples, round all around, protruding around the central branch, in the manner made for the candelabra of nobles, and they are called פומיל\"ש בְּלַעַז, and their number is written in the passage — how many knobs protrude from it and how much space between knob and knob." "<b>And its flowers.</b> Designs fashioned in it like flowers." "<b>Of it they shall be.</b> All of beaten work, emerging from within the block of gold; he shall not make them separately and attach them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French souldier/soudier, 'silversmith/goldsmith'", 1 "the la'az is Old French beté/esté or similar, 'hammer-stroke'; the exact Old French word is uncertain", 5 "the la'az מדיר\"נש is Old French medirenos, a type of long narrow goblet", 6 "the la'az פומיל\"ש is Old French pommeau, a knob/boss shaped like a small apple"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:40.517723006Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}